# K03 NS-ROLES-CALL control (v3 M2; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:304, :398): explicit `call: Model` -- twice at the root,
# once in a method, once retained in Outer's body and run by `call: Outer` -- executes Model's body; `Model()`,
# `Model: ()` and bare `Model` are not calls; defining Outer runs nothing.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: hits 0
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
end: Model
Outer:
    call: Model
end: Outer
call: Model
call: Model
fn: m () int
    call: Model
    call: Outer
    if: node\hits != 4
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
